+### Proposed, awaiting the steward: agents propose changes of intent rather than make them
+
+**Status**: Proposal, not a decision. Raised 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment run in plan mode. Answers open question Q2 in `TODO.md`.
+**Context**: The `INTENT.md` preamble says it is "meant to be refined collaboratively — by humans and AI agents". `AGENTS.md` "Consult INTENT.md for significant decisions" tells a session to update `INTENT.md` when a decision refines or challenges it, and the local guard used to say the same. Nothing records who may decide a change of intent, so a session can change the north star to fit its own work.
+**Proposal**: A session may correct `INTENT.md` where a recorded decision already settles the point, citing it. A change to what the project is for is recorded here as a proposal for the steward, and `INTENT.md` changes only after the steward's recorded decision. If adopted, amend the preamble and the `AGENTS.md` practice to say so.
+**Impact if adopted**: The repo's own instructions and the intent-change rule in `skills/local/entropy-guard/SKILL.md` agree.
+
+---
+
+### Proposed, awaiting the steward: one skill writes guards
+
+**Status**: Proposal, not a decision. Raised 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment run in plan mode. Answers open question Q3 in `TODO.md`.
+**Context**: `skills/docs-first-planning-assessment/` has "Phase 2: Guard Generation / Refinement". `skills/session-coherence-skill-generator/` writes `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md` from its own template. `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" gives the generator role to the assessment workflow, including `docs-first-planning-assessment`, and does not mention `session-coherence-skill-generator`. `README.md` describes both. No entry here records why the generator joined the exported skills or how the two relate.
+**Proposal**: Make `session-coherence-skill-generator` the only skill that writes guards. `docs-first-planning-assessment` supplies its checks and hands over. Reason: the newest entry below already invests in the generator, and it carries the one written guard template. Then reduce the other skill, `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" and `README.md` "To generate guards" to links.
+**Impact if adopted**: External users meet one generator and one template, and `INTENT.md` names the skill that does the job.
+
